~ ending_style
You reach the after life. It’s soft and ethereal, as if you’ve returned to your home’s skies. You jump around on the soft puffs – clouds – you remember what they’re named.
You lie down in one and let yourself become consumed in its tenderness. It’s like the nicest bed you’ve ever laid in.
Every once in a while, you wake up and bounce around from cloud to cloud. You admire the beautiful colours and textures. You never feel bored and yet you never feel quite energetic either. You feel an everlasting sense of calm.
=> END

~ ending_sturdiness
You reach the after life. You’re atop an old, sturdy tree, surrounded by equally sturdy trees. Looking below, you can see how far you are from the ground, and yet the fear of you falling down and hurting yourself never comes.
Some trees are shorter than others, some taller, though you are not sure exactly how far they go.
You are always able to look up and see the sky, and yet there seems like another tree you can climb, their branches reaching out at you as if encouraging you to take their path.
You soon learn to swing on the vines, feeling the cool wind surrounding you as you do. The trees grow the sweetest and most filling berries, making you content. You never reach the grand skies and you don’t want to.
The trees are your new home.
=> END

~ ending_size
You’re in a neighbourhood of houses, however its houses are all empty. You don’t mind, however, it’s fun to explore! You enjoy exploring the neighbourhoods that span forever, finding empty parks, abandoned malls.
It gets lonely after a while, though not for long. Soon, an older man appears, his hairs gray and back hunched over. Despite his appearance, though, he is nimble and able to easily catch up to you, even if you run.
You don’t remember him, and he doesn’t remember you, all you know is that you can trust each other.
Soon after, you both encounter an older woman, she seems to trust both you and the older man, and the three of you explore everything this world has to offer.
You enjoy the outdoors as vines and other greenery seem to slowly consume all of the buildings, the three of you, as a family for eternity.
=> END

~ ending_death
You throw all your memories in the river Lethe.
You are consumed by the river, you lose yourself until you are indistinguishable from the pale waters.
=> END

~ ending_lost
You are consumed by the river, you lose yourself until you are indistinguishable from the pale waters.
